# The names this repository may use, and what each is.
#
# Every name in the tree that stands for something in Second Life -- an
# avatar, a region, a parcel, a group, a landmark, an object or an
# inventory item -- is invented, and is written down here.  A name that is
# not here is refused by tools/check-identities wherever it can be
# recognised (doc/identities.md lists the places).  Nobody can tell a real
# name from a convincing invention, so the rule is the other way round: a
# name comes in by being added here, and a new one is taken from the
# spares at the end first.
#
# An invention need not match a real place one for one, and must not be a
# real resident, region, parcel, group or object.  The Example family
# (Example Resident, Example Builders, ...) and the Test... names are the
# mark of an invention here, as 7e57 is for ids.  Two kinds are the only
# real ones allowed: the owner's own (Quark Idlemind, qi, his group) and
# Linden Lab's published names (its sandboxes, parcel names, standard
# folders); each says why beside it.
#
# Matching ignores case and treats Rue&amp;Reed and Rue&Reed alike.  A
# name given as a search key may be the start of a name or of one of its
# words, and a first or last name may be one word of one; neither needs a
# line of its own.
#
# One per line: the name, a tab, what it is or why it may be here.

